      },
      "message": "docs(data): add descriptions for Zve* and Zvl*b extensions\n\nReplace TBD placeholder descriptions with accurate documentation for the\nembedded vector extensions and vector register length extensions:\n\nZvl*b extensions (Zvl32b, Zvl64b, Zvl128b, Zvl256b, Zvl512b, Zvl1024b):\n- Specify minimum vector register length (VLEN) requirements\n- Document the VLMAX calculations for each VLEN setting\n- Note that Zvl128b is the minimum required by the full V extension\n\nZve*x/f/d extensions:\n- Zve32x: Integer-only vector operations with ELEN=32\n- Zve32f: Adds single-precision FP to Zve32x\n- Zve64x: Integer-only vector operations with ELEN=64\n- Zve64f: Adds single-precision FP to Zve64x\n- Zve64d: Adds double-precision FP to Zve64f\n\nAll descriptions are based on the RISC-V Vector Extension specification\nversion 1.0.\n\nCloses #616\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>",
